<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS CUTS RATES ON PERSONAL LOANS.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS CUTS RATES ON PERSONAL LOANS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will keep its base</p>
<p>lending rates unchanged for one week effective February 11 but</p>
<p>it will cut its personal loan rate by 100 basis points and the</p>
<p>rate on installment loans with invoices by 200 basis points.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 16.75 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 17.50 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 17 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 16 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 23 from 24 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 21 from 23</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 18.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  7.99 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.70 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  2.93 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.55 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.58 percent</p>
<p>Pounds Sterling:  9.06 percent</p>
<p>French francs  :  5.81 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.46 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
